// Adventuring parties that come to town during a round (PartySystem). They're neutral: nobody
// fights them, and they treat everyone as the help. "adventurerKinds" are the members: gear,
// Melee/Shooting skill range, the silver coins they arrive with, and "spend": how free they are
// with it (what a service is worth to them is its worth in services.json times this); "tastes":
// what they like in a meal, said ordering it (Hospitality.Tastes: Savoury, Sweet, Hot, Fresh). "parties"
// are who travels together, where they loiter ("haunt", a town role: the Tavern) and how many game hours
// they stay (±25%). A "traveller" party is one person passing through, not adventuring: they come
// of an afternoon (PartySystem's own schedule), stay "nightsMin".."nightsMax" nights and never quest.
// "tempers": how likely each kind is to be Easy, Rowdy, Picky, Stingy, Boastful or Timid
// (Adventurers/Tempers: what a service is worth to them, how long they'll wait, how thirsty, how
// fussy, what they say). "folk": what they always are (Dwarf, Halfling, Elf; else the look's own
// pick); "look": what's fixed about how they look ("body", "hair", "beard" by name, "hairColor" as hex;
// the rest derived). A helm goes on over the outfit and takes the Head slot, so an outfit with a hood
// is for a kind without one. Names are our own; keep tabletop terms out.
//
// A "rare" company comes now and then (PartySystem: "chance" in a round, on a day from "fromDay"
// to "toDay", in place of the next party; one a round at most). Its "members" always come, its
// "extraMembers" join as the round has more players, none at "coreAt" (4) and all at "fullAt" (12),
// so a full company only comes to a town big enough for it. "fixedNames": each member's name is the
// one in the same place. A company may have its own errand (quests.json "party"): it's posted when
// they come, and it's the only quest they'll take.
